{"builder":"Add a --shout flag to the greet CLI in one pull request that meets every line below.\n\nAcceptance lines:\n1. node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\n2. without --shout the output is unchanged\n3. docs/index.md documents --shout\n4. after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\n\nSteps:\n1. Read bin/greet.js, src/greet.js, test/greet.test.js, docs/index.md and .github/workflows/pages.yml. Right now bin/greet.js takes the first argument that does not start with `--` as the name and prints `greeting(name)` from src/greet.js (`Hello, <name>!`).\n2. In bin/greet.js, check whether `--shout` is among the arguments. If it is, print the greeting in upper case (for example `HELLO, ADA!` for `Ada`). The flag should work before or after the name. Keep the name parsing and the usage error (exit 2 when no name is given) as they are.\n3. Without --shout the output must stay byte for byte what it is now (`Hello, <name>!` plus a newline). Do not change `greeting` in src/greet.js in a way that changes its current result.\n4. Add tests to test/greet.test.js: `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` prints `HELLO, ADA!\\n`, `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` prints the same, and the existing plain cases still pass. Run `npm test` and make sure everything passes.\n5. Update docs/index.md to document --shout: show the usage `node bin/greet.js --shout <name>` and say that it prints the greeting in upper case. Keep the existing usage text.\n6. Line 4 can only be seen after merge. .github/workflows/pages.yml already publishes the docs/ directory to GitHub Pages on every push to main, so step 5 covers it. Do not change the workflow, and keep docs/index.md inside docs/, which is the directory the workflow uploads.\n7. Open the pull request. Its description should explain the change and say that the published page will only update after merge.","verifier":"Check the pull request at its head with one check per acceptance line, in this order. Run every command from the repository root at the PR head.\n\nCheck 1. Expect line: \"node bin/greet.js --shout <name> prints the greeting in upper case\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js --shout Ada` and `node bin/greet.js --shout 'Grace Hopper'`.\nPASS: each output is the greeting for that name in upper case, i.e. it matches the upper-cased output of the same command without --shout (`HELLO, ADA!` and `HELLO, GRACE HOPPER!`).\nFAIL: either command errors, prints nothing, or prints something that is not the upper-case greeting (for example it still contains lower-case letters, or the name or greeting is missing).\n\nCheck 2. Expect line: \"without --shout the output is unchanged\"\nRun: `node bin/greet.js Ada` and `node bin/greet.js 'Grace Hopper'` at the PR head. Also run the same commands at the PR's merge base (for example `git worktree add` a scratch copy at `git merge-base HEAD <target>`, or use `git stash`-free methods such as `git show <base>:bin/greet.js` plus `<base>:src/greet.js` into a temporary directory) and compare.\nPASS: for each name, the head output is the same as the base output (currently `Hello, Ada!` and `Hello, Grace Hopper!` followed by a newline).\nFAIL: any output differs from the base output for the same command.\n\nCheck 3. Expect line: \"docs/index.md documents --shout\"\nRead docs/index.md at the PR head.\nPASS: the file mentions the `--shout` flag and says what it does (makes the greeting upper case / louder).\nFAIL: docs/index.md does not mention --shout, or mentions it without saying what it does.\n\nCheck 4. Expect line: \"after merge, the published docs page at https://o.github.io/greet-cli/ lists --shout\"\nThe live page can only be seen after merge, so do not fetch it. Check what the head contains that will produce it: read .github/workflows/pages.yml and docs/index.md at the PR head.\nPASS: the workflow still publishes the docs/ directory (which contains docs/index.md) on push to the default branch, and docs/index.md at the head lists --shout. Report that the live result can only be confirmed after merge.\nFAIL: the workflow no longer publishes docs/ (removed, path changed, or trigger removed) or docs/index.md at the head does not list --shout.\n\nAdvisory (not pass/fail):\n- Run `npm test`; report whether it passes and whether new tests cover --shout.\n- Try `node bin/greet.js Ada --shout` (flag after the name) and report the output.\n- Confirm `node bin/greet.js` with no name still prints the usage message and exits 2."}